Let's double-check direct derivation of a_{i+6}=a_i for any i using only recurrence valid for all i. Since indices mod n, recurrence a_{j+1}=a_j/a_{j-1} for all j. For any fixed i:
a_{i+1}=a_i/a_{i-1}
a_{i+2}=a_{i+1}/a_i=1/a_{i-1}
a_{i+3}=a_{i+2}/a_{i+1}=1/a_i
a_{i+4}=a_{i+3}/a_{i+2}=a_{i-1}/a_i
a_{i+5}=a_{i+4}/a_{i+3}=a_{i-1}
a_{i+6}=a_{i+5}/a_{i+4}=a_i.
All divisions valid nonzero. Good. This uses a_{i-1} known nonzero. Indices mod n, no problem.
